{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1162","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1162","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1162\",\"parent_revision\":\"376a7e0cc735a60fadeaa82855fdec95bca499bd\",\"root_revision\":\"e709de133c33ad04e7ffd94e5c3c0c04d6e59ae08d4353fe2800d63357352e81\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe Section model has a key (name) and content but no type indicator. For the progressive disclosure access pattern to work, agents need to determine which sections are relevant to their pipeline stage without loading section content first.\\n\\nA SectionType field on Section (or a well-known key registry mapping section names to pipeline stages) is the routing mechanism. Without it, an agent must either load all sections to find the relevant ones, or rely on section names matching a known convention \u2014 both of which are fragile.\\n\\nDiscovered during P964 implementation review (2026-03-31). The domain model change to add SectionType is the prerequisite for #1161 (agents using sections with progressive disclosure).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add sectiontype to section model to enable stage-based routing in progressive disclosure** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 fix-append-or-replace agent research, 2026-03-31\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Prerequisite for #1161 (progressive disclosure access pattern). Without SectionType, agents cannot implement stage-based section filtering, making all structured data in BacklogItem.sections invisible to the pipeline.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: #1161 (agents using sections with progressive disclosure)\\n- Bottleneck: Every agent in the pipeline that reads backlog items (groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item, rt-ica, feature-researcher) currently ignores sections entirely because there is no routing mechanism\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Enables agents to query \\\"which sections are relevant to my stage\\\" from the compact inventory, before spending context budget loading content\\n- Makes RT-ICA results, impact radius, learnings, and fact-check data discoverable and loadable on-demand\\n- Provides a stable contract between section producers (agents that write sections) and consumers (agents that read them)\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `backlog_view` is called with `include_content=False`, the returned `sections_metadata` list includes a `section_type` field on each entry. A grooming agent checks for `section_type == \\\"grooming\\\"` entries; a planning agent checks for `section_type == \\\"planning\\\"` entries. Neither agent loads sections typed for other stages.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA `SectionType` StrEnum in `backlog_core/models.py` with values covering the known pipeline stages. `SectionMeta` gains a `section_type: SectionType` field. A registry (constant dict or function) maps well-known section heading patterns (e.g. `\\\"Groomed\\\"`, `\\\"RT-ICA\\\"`, `\\\"Fact Check\\\"`, `\\\"Learnings\\\"`, `\\\"Impact Radius\\\"`) to their `SectionType`. `_build_sections_compact` in `operations.py` populates `section_type` on each `SectionMeta` entry using the registry, defaulting to a `CUSTOM` or `UNKNOWN` value for unrecognized headings.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `SectionType` StrEnum exists in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` with at least these values: `grooming`, `planning`, `verification`, and `custom` (or `unknown`)\\n2. `SectionMeta` in `models.py` includes a `section_type` field typed as `SectionType`\\n3. A registry mapping section heading patterns to `SectionType` values exists in `models.py` or a dedicated registry module \u2014 covers at minimum: `Groomed`, `RT-ICA`, `Fact Check`, `Learnings`, `Impact Radius`, `Acceptance Criteria`\\n4. `_build_sections_compact` in `operations.py` populates `section_type` on each returned dict using the registry\\n5. `backlog_view(include_content=False)` response includes `section_type` on each entry in `sections_metadata`\\n6. Unit tests assert that known heading names map to expected `SectionType` values and that unknown headings map to `CUSTOM`/`UNKNOWN`\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py (Section model, SectionMeta at line 529, ViewItemResult.sections at line 526) |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py (_build_sections_compact at line 1681, _build_sections_metadata at line 1636) |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py (extract_sections at line 717) |\\n| Issue | #1161 \u2014 downstream consumer item (agents using progressive disclosure) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: #1161 (agents not updated to use BacklogItem.sections \u2014 progressive disclosure access pattern missing)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The Section model change (adding a field to `SectionMeta` and a StrEnum) is contained to `models.py`. The registry lookup is a constant dict lookup in `_build_sections_compact`. No schema migrations, no database changes. Risk is in choosing the right SectionType values and heading-pattern registry to cover current usage without over-engineering.\\n\",\"digest\":\"c0a8834d5fb3c9d262bb4f55f6386106585445af6e283c7ed339fb9f93e9ff3c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg5tew\"}"}